om7w&_nc_zt=3&_nc_ht=scontent-ord5-2.oculuscdn.com&_nc_ss=8&oh=00_Afxdm4vE3K9FgVrhGa0HDaBBMJJ5nC7mVXMoHeGZGgH0Pg&oe=69B94235"}], "video_trailer": null, "video_trailer_thumbnail": {"file_name": "AED Use Training_Landscape.png", "id": "1731682440686153", "uri": "https://scontent-ord5-3.oculuscdn.com/v/t64.5771-25/38982681_1731682444019486_4602137284528913229_n.png?_nc_cat=106&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=6e7a0a&_nc_ohc=U-ULDB1rBGMQ7kNvwHLdKTD&_nc_oc=Adl15qQKCMeESRaSSLPO9bB4fe4_bD9w0kWCn4jK8CANA6vSdWWrPsrvPbbbuZFjnF0&_nc_zt=3&_nc_ht=scontent-ord5-3.oculuscdn.com&_nc_ss=8&oh=00_AfzxjerlwCeKZe8CPa00M4FzvTc3S5cJlby0STn9V6cKLw&oe=69B934F8"}, "display_name": "AED Use Training - ContentsDA", "keywords": ["safety", "aed", "cpr", "simulation", "contentsda"], "long_description": "1. Check for consciousness: Approach the collapsed person and determine if they are conscious.\n2. Establish an airway: If the person is conscious, support their neck and tilt their chin back to establish an airway.\n3. What to do if unconscious: If the person is not breathing, call 911 and describe the situation.\n4. Prepare to use an AED: Locate and move to the nearest AED box.\n5. Apply the AED: Place the AED near the collapsed person and press the power button to activate the machine.\n6. Apply patches: Unbutton the person's shirt and place the AED patches over the right chest and next to the left chest.\n7. Shock: Press the defibrillation button to deliver an electric shock, keeping your distance from the victim.\n8. CPR: Continue CPR after defibrillation, using two hands at a rate of 100 compressions per minute.\n9. Check and repeat: Ends if the patient regains consciousness, but if they don't improve, check their condition and repeat the entire process if necessary.", "short_description": "Learn how to use an Automated External Defibrillator (AED). This life-saving skill is essential in emergency situations where someone is experiencing cardiac arrest."}]}, "developer_name": null, "developer_privacy_policy_u